Z||000000||trigger||10-15-2000||08:55 PM||||one of the previous owners of my car smoked and I can't get rid of the smell.  I thought I got rid of it, when I bought the car.  You could only get a sniff of it once in a while.  Well, lately it's been horrible.  Does anybody have any ideas on how to get rid of it.  Thanks.<P>------------------<BR>Honestly officer, I was just keeping up with the flow of traffic.  I know there aren't any cars in the area, that's how far behind I am.||||reg||8
Z||000001||Seanh||10-15-2000||08:59 PM||||Fabreez, Cleans bad smells out of fabrics for good.<P>------------------<BR>Sean Heberly<BR>Silver 86 GT 2.8<BR>Killer Stereo System||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||10-15-2000||09:05 PM||||Try love-my-carpet or similar product on the carpets too.<BR>Fabreeze is awesome!!<P>------------------<BR>Jeff<BR>85GT||||reg||1
Z||000003||Hank is Here||10-15-2000||09:13 PM||||Try renting an ozone generator. I did this in another car for a damp smell and it took care of it (well at least till it got wet again)<P>Mark Johnson<p>[This message has been edited by Hank is Here (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000004||Tigger||10-15-2000||09:31 PM||||I used a portable steam vac on my seats.  Worked great and the detergent (I can't remember the name off hand) made them smell like they were new.<P>I noticed with my car that there was a ton of ash that had fallen in under the center console.  Check under yours that might be where some of the smell might be coming from.<P>------------------<BR>T-T-F-N, Tah Tah For Now!<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/tigger.gif">           <BR>  <A HREF="mailto:RacingStripes@hotmail.com">RacingStripes@hotmail.com</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Jaygee79||10-15-2000||09:49 PM||||If you can find a way to get rid of it, let me know.  I let my mom borrow my car 3 years ago (she smokes) and to this day the smell of smoke is still there.||||reg||1
Z||000006||fiero56||10-15-2000||09:59 PM||||Both of my Fieros had previous owners that smoked. I thoroughly steam vacced them both, and fabreezed EVERYTHING. I took out the seats, sprayed all carpet, headliner, sun visors, everything. The '88 I have had for over a year, and the smell has never come back. The '86 was just cleaned out today, but the smell is gone for now, hopefully forever.<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pffsig1.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 10-15-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||theogre||10-15-2000||10:44 PM||||Definatly look under the ash trays. There's likely all sorts of trash down there. You'll need to pull at least the center secion of the consol(the part around the shifter) to get it all out.||||reg||1
Z||000008||286SE'S||10-16-2000||11:49 AM||||I third the recommendation for Fabreez.<BR>My neice gave me small sofa cause her boyfriend smoked and it really stunk. I had planned to keep it in the garage for a thinking couch but it stunk too much. Soaked it with a whole bottle of Fabreez and it <BR>never stank again. It went into the house that winter and no smoke smell at all, even if you stick your nose right up close!||||reg||1
Z||000009||stsmithgt||10-16-2000||12:32 PM||||I support the steamcleaning on a hot day so it will dry or put a fan in it. and fourth the motion for the Frebreez. Don't forget to spray headliner.  I put that Frebreez through a buddies portable swamp cooler that smelled less than desirable.  It smelled MUCH better after the treatment.  I haven't tried it on smoke so that's all I have to offer. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000010||My7Fieros||10-16-2000||08:19 PM||||Yeah...start smoking..then you wont notice the smell!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>||||reg||1
